From: Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 07:02:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 52/59] drm/panthor: memory usage in fdinfo

Panthor fds on 6.12 print no memory lines in fdinfo. Steam ARM's
renderer check (drm_fd_used) reads drm-total/drm-resident lines to tell
a GPU client from an llvmpipe process that only probed the render node;
without them every holder of renderD130 counts as a GPU client. nvtop
and gputop read the same keys.

Port the mainline memory accounting carried by the 6.1 rkr7.2
backport: a gem .status hook (imported or backed by pages = resident)
so drm_show_memory_stats() prints drm-{total,shared,active,resident}
-memory, plus panthor-{resident,active}-memory for kernel BOs the file
owns indirectly (group suspend buffers, sync objects, ring buffers,
queue interfaces, profiling slots, tiler heap chunks and heap
contexts). Heap pools keep a running size; group sizes are summed
before the group becomes visible in the pool. drm_fdinfo_print_size()
is not exported on 6.12, so the driver formats the two lines itself.
panthor 1.5 port, 8.0p15.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
